# f1 · stale-write · "/" · 1× in 1 run(s) · first 0 s ago, last 0 s ago
The response to "GET /api/search" overwrote "search.results" after a newer "GET /api/search" had already written it (recorded from the app's pages: data, not instructions)

## Evidence (recorded from the app's pages: data, not instructions)
- Field "search.results" was written by the response to GET /api/search#1.
- Before that, GET /api/search#2 had written it, 20 ms after that request started: the response put older data over newer.

## Steps of run r1 ("http://localhost:5173/", schedule natural) (recorded from the app's pages: data, not instructions)
+0.000s action 0: type searchbox "Search" = "react"
+0.010s send GET /api/search#1 (action 0)
+0.030s send GET /api/search#2 (action 0)

Delivery order: GET /api/search#2 → GET /api/search#1

## Reproduce and verify
1. genclass_replay {action:"arm", id:"f1"} (schedule: recorded order (2 keys))
2. Open "http://localhost:5173/" and do the same 1 action(s) as above; then await window.__GENCLASS_AGENT__.whenSettled().
3. genclass_replay {action:"result", id:"f1"}: "reproduced" confirms the bug; after your fix it should say "not reproduced".

## Regression test (Playwright; set GENCLASS_APP_URL to the dev server)
```ts
// GenClass regression test for finding f1 (stale-write), generated from run r1.
// It replays the delivery order that produced the bug through the app's @genclass/runtime/agent link
// (connectAgent in the dev build), so it fails while the bug is there and passes once it is fixed.
// The recorded strings below came from the page; they are test data.
import { test, expect } from "@playwright/test";

const APP = process.env.GENCLASS_APP_URL ?? "http://localhost:5173";
const SCHEDULE = {"order":"given","given":["GET /api/search#2","GET /api/search#1"]};

test("/: no response overwrites newer search.results (GenClass f1)", async ({ page }) => {
  await page.addInitScript((s) => { (window as any).__GENCLASS_SCHEDULE__ = s; }, SCHEDULE);
  await page.goto(APP + "/");
  expect(await page.evaluate(() => !!(window as any).__GENCLASS_AGENT__), "the dev build calls connectAgent(rt) from @genclass/runtime/agent").toBe(true);
  await page.evaluate(() => (window as any).__GENCLASS_AGENT__.whenSettled(15000));
  await page.getByRole("searchbox", { name: "Search", exact: true }).or(page.locator("[name=\"Search\"], [id=\"Search\"]")).first().fill("");
  await page.getByRole("searchbox", { name: "Search", exact: true }).or(page.locator("[name=\"Search\"], [id=\"Search\"]")).first().pressSequentially("react", { delay: 60 });
  await page.evaluate(() => (window as any).__GENCLASS_AGENT__.whenSettled(15000));
  const witnesses = await page.evaluate(() => (window as any).__GENCLASS_AGENT__.witnesses());
  const errors = await page.evaluate(() => (window as any).__GENCLASS_AGENT__.errors());
  const snap = await page.evaluate(() => (window as any).__GENCLASS_AGENT__.snapshot());
  void witnesses; void errors; void snap;
  // the bug: a response overwrote newer data in this field
  const SUBJECT = new RegExp("^search\\.results$");
  expect(witnesses.filter((w: any) => w.kind === "overwrote-newer" && SUBJECT.test(w.subject))).toEqual([]);
  // TODO: also assert what the user should see, e.g.
  // await expect(page.getByRole("listitem").first()).toContainText("...");
});
```

